<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Rain seen over southern Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Rain seen over southern Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Saturday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		    54.5</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     59</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   12</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  57.6</p>
<p>    Moussakele		64.8</p>
<p>    Norton		    40.8</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    23</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   4.5</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department forecasts occasional showers in the Central, Sabaragamuwa, Western and Southern provinces and over the sea off the south and west coasts, with fairly strong gusty winds.</p>
</text>
